    14	Parametric fuzzing combines evolutionary and generator-based
    15	fuzzing to create structured test inputs that exercise unique execution behaviors. Parametric fuzzers internally represent inputs as bit
    16	strings referred to as “parameter sequences”. Interesting parameter
    17	sequences are saved by the fuzzer and perturbed to create new inputs without the need for type-specific operators. However, existing
    18	work on parametric fuzzing only uses mutation operators, which
    19	modify a single input; it does not incorporate crossover, an evolutionary operator that blends multiple inputs together. Crossover
    20	operators aim to combine advantageous traits from multiple inputs.
    21	However, the nature of parametric fuzzing limits the effectiveness
